{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1491016-blocking-influence","id":1491016,"title":"Blocking Influence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-22T11:51:22-07:00","id":1491016,"title":"Blocking Influence","content":"I have read the rules for Blocking Influence on page 89 in the Trinity Corebook three times, and I am still stumped on exactly how to adjudicate this in play.<br /> <br /> My core issue is -<br /> <br /> It starts by saying that if a character refuses the Influence of another character, the character doing the Influencing receives a Consolation of 1 Enhancement if the influence is refused, or 3 Enhancement if the influence is actively acted against.<br /> <br /> It then says that if the Influencing character is a player character, instead of Enhancement, they receive Momentum. Ok, so far so good.<br /> <br /> It then closes by saying that Storyguide characters do not receive Consolation.<br /> <br /> So what scenario is the first paragraph referring to? If Player Characters always receive Momentum, what was all that stuff about 1 or 3 Enhancement? Who receives that? It seems like the first and last paragraph directly contradict each other - but if so, which one is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:50:07-07:00","id":1491027,"title":"","content":"Storyguides, when trying to influence you, dont gain consolation.<br /> <br /> The first line is refering to a PC influencing a SGC and the second when a PC is influencing another PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-